.TH PHPVPN-SERVICE 8 "2026-10-30" "phpvpn 1.0.3" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
phpvpn-service \- phpvpn client service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/libexec/phpvpn/phpvpn-service
.RB [ \-\-systemd " | " \-\-foreground " | " \-\-console " | " \-\-verify\-tunnel ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phpvpn-service
owns the phpvpn configuration, the TUN interface
.BR phpvpn ,
its VPN address and single on-link route, the authenticated relay session and
the VPN state. The default route and DNS are never changed (split tunnel).
Clients such as
.BR phpvpn (1)
and the tray talk to it over the public control socket.
.PP
It normally runs as the systemd unit
.BR phpvpn.service .
The unit runs it as root with only
.B CAP_NET_ADMIN
and a sandbox; it restarts after a failure (5 s, about 17 s, then 60 s).
When
.B autoConnectOnStartup
is true in the configuration, the service connects after it reported readiness.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-systemd
Run under systemd with
.BR Type=notify :
READY=1 once the control socket listens, a STATUS= line with the connection
state and STOPPING=1 on shutdown. Log records go to the journal through
standard error. This is the default when
.B NOTIFY_SOCKET
is set.
.TP
.BR \-\-foreground ", " \-\-console
Run in the foreground with log lines on standard output until SIGINT
(Ctrl+C) or SIGTERM. Creates the runtime directory when it is missing. The
default without
.BR NOTIFY_SOCKET .
Requires root.
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-tunnel
Check that
.I /dev/net/tun
is the kernel TUN device offering IFF_TUN and IFF_NO_PI and print its
features and the kernel release. Creates no interface.
.PP
SIGTERM and SIGINT stop the service: the connection is torn down, the route,
address and interface are removed, then the process exits. SIGHUP is ignored.
Only one instance runs at a time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/phpvpn/config.json
Configuration, directory 0700 and file 0600, owned by root.
.TP
.I /var/lib/phpvpn/ownership.json
Ownership journal of the tunnel interface, used for recovery after a crash.
.TP
.I /run/phpvpn/control-v1.sock
Public control socket, mode 0666.
.TP
.I /run/phpvpn/service.lock
Singleton lock.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B journalctl \-u phpvpn
shows the service log,
.B phpvpn diagnostics
the extended local diagnostics.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phpvpn (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemd.exec (5)
